cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GroundTruth-Geo: A deterministic, government-cited benchmark of parcel-precise US property facts"
message: "If you use this benchmark or the accompanying grader / MCP server in academic work or model evaluation, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Sullivan
    given-names: Tim
    website: "https://lastingground.com"
abstract: >-
  GroundTruth-Geo is a machine-gradable benchmark of parcel-precise US
  property facts on the exact questions frontier large language models fail
  on geography (GPSBench / MapEval: under 25% on parcel geometry, 1–23% on
  city-level localization). Each item is a deterministic government record
  cited to FEMA / NPS / EPA with an official source URL, a source date, and
  a reproducible content fingerprint. The repository ships a deterministic
  grader using field-standard factuality metrics (SimpleQA F1,
  AA-Omniscience Index) and a JSON-RPC stdio MCP server exposing the
  records as agent tools. No LLM is in the answer path — the verifier is
  external government ground truth and is, by construction, ungameable.
repository-code: "https://github.com/sulmusic2-star/groundtruth-geo"
url: "https://github.com/sulmusic2-star/groundtruth-geo"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - factuality
  - large-language-models
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp-server
  - llm-evaluation
  - geospatial
  - deterministic-verifier
references:
